2 - let's connect to the IDE (AWS Cloud9) on the EC2 instance 
AWS Cloud9 is a service you can run on an EC2 instance which provides an IDE that includes features like Code editor , debugger and terminal 
note : you don't need to download a key pair to connect to IDE  
3 - so in the search write Cloud 9 
Advice : learn how to create Cloud9 as it is simple not hard 
but some tips to create it 
A - ensure that it is ubuntu or Amazon Linux 2 
B - ensure that SSH permission are accessible by existing key pair 
C - ensure that the security group allows to reach EC2 to Cloud9 
D - ensure that EC2 has the agent of SSM to connect to the Cloud9
when you open it , you will see a screen like the terminal 

Task 2 let's analyzing the LAMP stack environment and confirming that the web server is accessible 
A - first observe the OS version in the AWS Cloud9 bash terminal by writing :
cat /proc/version
the output will appear ( linux version 6.1.141-165.249.amzn2023........)(Red Hat 11.5.0-5) 
B- to observe the web server , PHP details , and server state, run this command :
sudo httpd -v
service httpd status 
php --version

the output shows the version of the web server and notice they are not running now 

4 - to start the web server , install the database and set them to start automatically after any future EC2 instance restart , run this command 
sudo chkconfig httpd on
sudo service httpd start
sudo service httpd status
#verify database
sudo mariadb --version
sudo systemctl enable mariadb
#
sudo chkconfig mariadb on
sudo service mariadb start
sudo service mariadb status

5 - to configure the EC2 instance so you can use AWS Cloud9 to edit the web server files , run this command :
ln -s /var/www/ /home/ec2-user/environment
sudo chown ec2-user:ec2-user /var/www/html

A - the first command creates a symlink from the default AWS Cloud9 editor workspace to the /var/www directory that contains your web server files 

B - the second command changes the ownership of the HTML subdirectory so that the ec2-user can edit and create new files in it 
